/* Small status/decoration icons for theme_osf_modern.c, replacing the
 * earlier LV_SYMBOL_WARNING glyph (error) and hand-drawn primitive (headlight)
 * with real vector icon designs, plus a new thermometer icon for the hero
 * motor-temp readout. Source icons (Iconify, MIT-licensed):
 *   - icon_headlight:   mingcute:low-beam-headlights-fill
 *   - icon_error:       tdesign:error-triangle-filled
 *   - icon_thermometer: streamline-ultimate:temperature-thermometer-medium
 *
 * Stored as LV_IMG_CF_ALPHA_4BIT (16 alpha levels, no inherent color - see
 * lv_img_decoder.c's built-in decoder: for ALPHA_* formats the actual pixel
 * color always comes from the target lv_obj's `img_recolor` style
 * (lv_obj_set_style_img_recolor()), not from anything stored here) rather
 * than a full-color format - these are single-color status icons, and
 * ALPHA_4BIT keeps flash cost minimal (roughly w*h/2 bytes) while still
 * letting each icon be tinted per its own on-screen meaning (blue for
 * lights-on, red for error, muted gray for the temp readout).
 *
 * Generated by rasterizing each icon's real SVG (fetched from
 * api.iconify.design, matching the exact icon IDs above) at 4x supersample
 * via a headless-browser canvas, box-downsampling to the target pixel size,
 * and packing the resulting per-pixel alpha into LVGL's documented
 * ALPHA_4BIT byte layout (2 pixels per byte, high nibble = even x) - a
 * one-off conversion, not a repeatable build step; re-run the same process
 * by hand if these icons ever need to change. */
#include "lvgl.h"

